title: Dead push branch in Client::build_image writes past Result read-only attributes
updated: 2026-08-27T04:06:55Z
---

build_image accepts a "push" option and calls _push_tags when set, but the
plugin never passes it - release() does its own tagging and pushing. The branch
is unreachable in production.

Worse, _push_tags mutates the Result object through its hash:

  $$result_ref->{digest} = ...
  push @{ $$result_ref->{pushed} }, $tag;

Result declares digest and pushed as is => ro with Types::Standard constraints;
writing through the hash bypasses both. If the branch is ever reached, it works
by accident.

Remove the branch and _push_tags, or route it through a proper constructor.

Fixed: the push argument, the if (push && tags) branch and _push_tags are removed from Client::build_image. build_image now returns the Result directly. Nothing called it - release() does its own tagging and pushing through push_image.
